  "id": "Compound::DB00449 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Dipivefrin is implicated in the regulation of Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity through its interaction with Adra2b, which participates in signaling pathways involving the Alpha-2 adrenergic receptor. This mechanism is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Dipivefrin binds to Adra2b, which in turn participates in processes that are ultimately linked to Adra2c. The evidence suggests that Dipivefrin may influence Adra2c through a shared pathway involving the Alpha-adrenergic receptor, potentially by modulating the activity of the receptor or its downstream signaling. The integration of these paths highlights a recurring mechanism where Dipivefrin's interaction with Adra2b contributes to the activation or regulation of Adra2c, likely through a common intermediary in the adrenergic signaling cascade. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, reinforcing the notion that Dipivefrin and Adra2c are connected via a shared biological process involving the Alpha-adrenergic receptor.",
